Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "publication_number": unique identifier of each patent; used to join citing and cited patents and to report final result.  
• "kind_code": filter to “…B2” to keep granted U.S. patents.  
• "country_code": filter to “US”.  
• "grant_date": filter to 2015‑01‑01 … 2018‑12‑31.  
• "citation": VARIANT array that contains the backward‑citation list (publications cited by the focal patent).  
• "ipc": VARIANT array that lists all IPC codes assigned to the publication; used to obtain 4‑digit IPC codes for cited patents.  

Typical conditions  
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'  
AND "kind_code" ILIKE '%B2'  
AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20150101 AND 20181231  

Ten exploratory ‑‑> final SQL statements  
```sql
--Description: 1) Inspect a handful of US‑B2 patents granted 2015‑2018.
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "kind_code",
  "grant_date",
  "country_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code" ILIKE '%B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20150101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Look at the raw structure of the "citation" array for one sample patent.
SELECT 
  f.value AS "citation_raw"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE p."publication_number" = 'US-YYYYYYY-B2'  -- replace with a real number after step 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Reveal keys inside an individual citation object.
SELECT 
  f.value:"publication_number"::STRING  AS "cited_pub_no",
  f.value:"category"::STRING            AS "cite_cat",
  f.value:"patent"::STRING              AS "cite_patent"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE p."publication_number" = 'US-YYYYYYY-B2'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Collect citing patent and all cited publication numbers (backward citations) for 2015‑2018 US‑B2 set.
SELECT 
  p."publication_number"          AS "citing_pub",
  f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" ILIKE '%B2'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20150101 AND 20181231
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Check IPC list for a cited patent to understand “ipc” structure.
SELECT 
  c."publication_number",
  ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING AS "ipc_full"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."ipc") ipc_u
WHERE c."publication_number" = 'US-XXXXXXX-A1'  -- pick any cited_pub from step 4
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Convert cited patent IPCs to 4‑digit codes.
SELECT 
  c."publication_number",
  SUBSTR(ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => c."ipc") ipc_u
WHERE c."publication_number" = 'US-XXXXXXX-A1'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) For each cited patent, deduplicate IPC4s and count occurrences.
SELECT 
  cited."publication_number" AS "cited_pub",
  SUBSTR(ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS cited,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => cited."ipc") ipc_u
WHERE cited."publication_number" IN ('US-XXXXXXX-A1', 'US-YYYYYYY-A1') -- sample list
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Aggregate cited‑IPC counts for every focal patent (step 4 join).
SELECT 
  rel."citing_pub",
  SUBSTR(ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4"
FROM (
    SELECT 
      p."publication_number" AS "citing_pub",
      f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
    FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
    WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
      AND p."kind_code" ILIKE '%B2'
      AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20150101 AND 20181231
) rel
JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS cited
  ON cited."publication_number" = rel."cited_pub",
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => cited."ipc") ipc_u
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Compute numerator (sum of squared IPC4 counts) and denominator (total IPC4)^2 per citing patent.
SELECT
  "citing_pub",
  SUM(POWER("ipc4_cnt", 2))           AS "sum_sq",
  POWER(SUM("ipc4_cnt"), 2)           AS "total_sq"
FROM (
    SELECT 
      rel."citing_pub",
      SUBSTR(ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
      COUNT(*) AS "ipc4_cnt"
    FROM (
        SELECT 
          p."publication_number" AS "citing_pub",
          f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
        WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
          AND p."kind_code" ILIKE '%B2'
          AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20150101 AND 20181231
    ) rel
    JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS cited
      ON cited."publication_number" = rel."cited_pub",
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => cited."ipc") ipc_u
    GROUP BY rel."citing_pub", SUBSTR(ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4)
) t
GROUP BY "citing_pub"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final query: compute ORIGINALITY and pick the US‑B2 patent (2015‑2018) with highest score.
SELECT
  base."citing_pub"                                AS "publication_number",
  1 - (SUM(POWER(cnt,2)) / POWER(SUM(cnt),2))      AS "originality_score"
FROM (
    SELECT 
      rel."citing_pub",
      SUBSTR(ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
      COUNT(*) AS cnt
    FROM (
        SELECT 
          p."publication_number" AS "citing_pub",
          f.value:"publication_number"::STRING AS "cited_pub"
        FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."citation") f
        WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
          AND p."kind_code" ILIKE '%B2'
          AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20150101 AND 20181231
    ) rel
    JOIN PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS cited
      ON cited."publication_number" = rel."cited_pub",
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => cited."ipc") ipc_u
    GROUP BY rel."citing_pub", SUBSTR(ipc_u.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4)
) base
GROUP BY base."citing_pub"
ORDER BY "originality_score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```
